Figure 1 illustrates the comparative adjuvanticity of Nano-11 and aluminum hydroxide (AH) by measuring anti-recombinant protective antigen (rPA) IgG titers in immunized mice. Soluble rPA alone elicits minimal antibody response. Both AH and Nano-11 significantly enhance rPA-specific IgG titers, with Nano-11 demonstrating comparable immunopotentiation to AH at higher doses (200 and 50 µg). Crucially, Nano-11 retains strong adjuvanticity at a lower dose of 12.5 µg, where AH fails to significantly boost the immune response, supporting Nano-11's effectiveness, particularly at low concentrations.